# Who the agent is, inside every Project's sandbox. The deploy seeds this file
# as ~/.sandcastle-vps/agent.env (never uploaded, never overwritten) and
# init-project / sync-env stamp it into each Project's .sandcastle/.env — the
# Harness itself never reads it (ADR 0003). Change something here, then run
# sync-env to push it to every Onboarded Project.

# Author of the agent's commits. The deploy pre-fills these from your machine's
# git config (falling back to your GitHub noreply address). Any address verified
# on your GitHub account works: signed agent commits then show as Verified
# under your account, with no second account involved.
AGENT_GIT_NAME=
AGENT_GIT_EMAIL=

# Fine-grained personal access token the agent uses to read issues, push Task
# Branches, and open pull requests. Scope it to the Project repositories only:
#   Contents: read and write · Pull requests: read and write
#   Issues: read and write   · Metadata: read
# https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
GH_TOKEN=

# The signing key is not in this file: the deploy generates
# ~/.sandcastle-vps/agent_signing_key (ed25519) next to it and prints the
# public half to register on GitHub as a signing key.
